Managing complexity is one of the most important things in what we do. Of course, before we can manage complexity, we need to be able to recognize it.

We humans are _really_ bad at this.


The problem is that *mastered things seem easy.*





Something is "simple" when it can be distilled down to a few thoughts that aren't intertwined with other concepts in complicated ways.

For example, playing a piano is simple, but not easy.



Using a framework is easy, but not simple.





